  "body": "Found while gating the #3173 PR on a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`. Environment-dependent test, not a behaviour change.\n\n## What happens\n\nA light-lane law test greps `AGENTS.md` for LF text. On a Windows checkout the file is checked out with CRLF, so the grep fails and the gate goes red for reasons that have nothing to do with the diff.\n\n## What the fix needs\n\n- The test (or the grep) must normalise line endings before it compares, so the law check is independent of `core.autocrlf`.\n- The same pattern check is owed to any other test that greps a tracked text file byte-for-byte.\n\n## Done means\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` is green on a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`, for the law test and any sibling grep test.\n\nObserved on 2026-11-22 during the #3173 gate (PR #3552).\n",
